  "Swazi Kingdom": "The Dlamini kingdom of Eswatini, founded in the 18th century, which survived colonial rule to become one of the world’s last absolute monarchies.",
  "Cape Colony": "Britain’s colony at the tip of Africa, whose frontier wars, abolition of slavery and Boer emigration shaped modern South Africa.",
  "Zulu Kingdom": "The kingdom Shaka built from a small chiefdom, whose regimental army dominated southeastern Africa and defeated Britain at Isandlwana.",
